\section{Attribution and remaining obligations}

The complete maximal subgroup classification is borrowed from Kleidman;
the natural line stabilizer description is borrowed from Wilson. The
original group, catalogue, orbit and transporter identifications and the
faithful form and frame are earlier inputs. The common projector argument
and the finite word construction are reused from the project's earlier
proofs. This note applies those arguments to eight newly acquired and
directly checked certificates.

Generation is only one requirement for these rank-four markings. Their
intersection property and final case dispositions remain to be proved.
This note adds no whole prefix, manuscript classification, open conjecture
resolution, Lean formalization or measured compression factor.

